00:56:48,711 --> 00:56:51,573
[SPEAKER_02]: Why is it usually in sutras it says the four great elements?

698
00:56:51,613 --> 00:56:52,674
[SPEAKER_02]: Why is it great?

699
00:56:52,894 --> 00:56:54,195
[SPEAKER_01]: Because they're so general.

700
00:56:55,135 --> 00:56:57,197
[SPEAKER_01]: So much in the background, it's the great.

701
00:56:57,937 --> 00:56:58,297
[SPEAKER_01]: Great.

702
00:56:58,317 --> 00:56:59,378
[SPEAKER_01]: The great elements, yeah.

703
00:57:00,026 --> 00:57:00,686
[SPEAKER_01]: Mahābhūta.

704
00:57:02,187 --> 00:57:05,229
[SPEAKER_01]: Mahābhūta is the power of spirit.

705
00:57:05,389 --> 00:57:10,192
[SPEAKER_01]: And your body being made out of those elements.

706
00:57:10,232 --> 00:57:17,836
[SPEAKER_01]: Again, as I said, your body is known as your body, because it's still living there.

707
00:57:19,097 --> 00:57:25,041
[SPEAKER_01]: Your body is known as such, because the body is there, as that because of which you can know that body.

708
00:57:25,781 --> 00:57:29,043
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, there is that resisting

709
00:57:29,490 --> 00:57:42,456
[SPEAKER_01]: The aspect to that body, the aspect that you can't even access, you can't even comprehend, because of which your body is aging, subject to elements change, disappearance, destruction, and so on.

710
00:57:43,637 --> 00:57:47,799
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's that extent of that resistance that comes from these elements.

711
00:57:48,359 --> 00:57:52,962
[SPEAKER_01]: But that is the... upon which your whole experience is actually founded.

712
00:57:52,982 --> 00:57:55,523
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you start to discern, you start to know,

713
00:57:56,267 --> 00:58:01,829
[SPEAKER_01]: That you're fully depending upon something you can't even think of and you can't even comprehend.

714
00:58:02,229 --> 00:58:04,150
[SPEAKER_01]: You just get the sense of it resisting you.

715
00:58:06,291 --> 00:58:07,151
[SPEAKER_01]: Hence resistance.

716
00:58:16,875 --> 00:58:17,796
[SPEAKER_01]: Means resistance.

717
00:58:21,937 --> 00:58:23,218
[SPEAKER_01]: Means not being in your control.

718
00:58:24,432 --> 00:58:26,954
[SPEAKER_01]: Means you can't even conceive it to be in your control.

719
00:58:27,774 --> 00:58:32,638
[SPEAKER_01]: It's... it's... it's offering... like means your... your... your volition, your will has its limits.

720
00:58:33,898 --> 00:58:35,559
[SPEAKER_01]: It can't reach its own foundations.

721
00:58:36,840 --> 00:58:37,721
[SPEAKER_01]: They're resisting it.

722
00:58:38,181 --> 00:58:43,105
[SPEAKER_01]: They're showing their own independence that you can't even change, you can't even... you can't even think of.

723
00:58:43,245 --> 00:58:47,487
[SPEAKER_02]: It is only for those who have self-involvement.

724
00:58:47,628 --> 00:58:48,028
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, no.

725
00:58:48,048 --> 00:58:49,769
[SPEAKER_01]: That's basically the four elements.

726
00:58:50,630 --> 00:58:52,511
[SPEAKER_01]: They find the footing in the experience.

727
00:58:52,957 --> 00:58:54,918
[SPEAKER_01]: For as long as there is ignorance present.

728
00:58:54,938 --> 00:59:03,300
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the arahant can talk about resistance, but there is nothing resisting it, or resisting him, or resisting in it, or out of it.

729
00:59:03,440 --> 00:59:03,660
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

730
00:59:04,961 --> 00:59:12,043
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just the four elements will remain sort of floating about, for as long as the five aggregates are there, and when he dies, that's it.

731
00:59:12,783 --> 00:59:15,204
[SPEAKER_01]: No more evil, because it's all broken up.

732
00:59:16,184 --> 00:59:21,906
[SPEAKER_01]: For ārya, again, there is sort of a bit of both, until all of the poison and toxins are cleared out.

733
00:59:23,747 --> 00:59:33,334
[SPEAKER_01]: But a Bhutujanite could be me, and then, whenever he needs the resistance, he will be resisting me, resisting in regard to me, I'm resisting it, I'm resisting it, out of it, whatever.

734
00:59:34,815 --> 00:59:35,636
[SPEAKER_02]: All right.

735
00:59:35,656 --> 00:59:37,157
[SPEAKER_01]: Means trying to control and...

736
00:59:37,177 --> 00:59:38,458
[SPEAKER_01]: Trying to control, yeah.

737
00:59:38,478 --> 00:59:39,099
[SPEAKER_02]: Yeah.

738
00:59:39,419 --> 00:59:39,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

739
00:59:40,079 --> 00:59:50,247
[SPEAKER_01]: But you want to recognize just that the foundations of your experience are that which resists you, because it can never even be taken up.

740
00:59:51,228 --> 00:59:52,649
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, you can't see directly

741
00:59:52,995 --> 00:59:54,096
[SPEAKER_01]: The four great elements.

742
00:59:56,018 --> 00:59:57,179
[SPEAKER_01]: They're always in the background.

743
00:59:58,580 --> 01:00:06,046
[SPEAKER_01]: The four great elements, as the foundation of this random body, is just... because what you see will be your perception.

744
01:00:06,627 --> 01:00:09,930
[SPEAKER_01]: And four great elements are determining your perception.

745
01:00:11,871 --> 01:00:14,694
[SPEAKER_01]: Which means you can't ever access them with that perception.

746
01:00:15,355 --> 01:00:18,077
[SPEAKER_01]: You can only know that your perception is there because of

747
01:00:19,932 --> 01:00:24,975
[SPEAKER_01]: That which, yeah, that which resists out there, that you can't even see.

748
01:00:29,437 --> 01:00:33,119
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, that's the designation.

749
01:00:33,219 --> 01:00:34,940
[SPEAKER_01]: Perception would be the designation.

750
01:00:35,300 --> 01:00:38,442
[SPEAKER_01]: What you can perceive, you can talk about, you can designate, you can think it.

751
01:00:39,743 --> 01:00:43,405
[SPEAKER_01]: But not that because of which that perception is there in the first place.

752
01:00:48,908 --> 01:00:52,310
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that which resists is what's being designated.

753
01:00:56,853 --> 01:01:00,175
[SPEAKER_01]: As that because of which designation is possible in the first place.

754
01:01:05,018 --> 01:01:16,726
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is all kind of a slightly more advanced way of saying that, fundamentally, things are completely out of your control, including your own sense of control.

755
01:01:19,273 --> 01:01:26,254
[SPEAKER_01]: Nobody's denying your sense of... Nobody's denying your sense of control.

756
01:01:27,374 --> 01:01:30,735
[SPEAKER_01]: What you want to realize is that you can't own even that.

757
01:01:32,635 --> 01:01:32,855
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

758
01:01:32,915 --> 01:01:37,216
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's fully founded upon that which is completely out of your hands.

759
01:01:43,017 --> 01:01:45,298
[SPEAKER_01]: Self is always in regard to that sense of control.

760
01:01:45,358 --> 01:01:45,538
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

761
01:01:47,255 --> 01:02:03,780
[SPEAKER_01]: So, once you start recognizing that your own sense of control is enclosed with this whole thing, that it's limiting you, then you realize that, well, even this control that I can exercise, modify things to an extent, I can't...

762
01:02:03,800 --> 01:02:04,440
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't hold it.

763
01:02:04,620 --> 01:02:08,482
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not permanent, because when its foundations go, it will all go.

764
01:02:11,983 --> 01:02:14,024
[SPEAKER_01]: But what's the role of concentration?

765
01:02:14,064 --> 01:02:16,044
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's part of the epochal...

766
01:02:16,064 --> 01:02:17,825
[SPEAKER_01]: Concentration is keeping things together.

767
01:02:18,165 --> 01:02:21,186
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, usually, people think concentration is focusing hard on one point.

768
01:02:21,286 --> 01:02:21,667
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

769
01:02:21,787 --> 01:02:21,947
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

770
01:02:22,147 --> 01:02:24,788
[SPEAKER_01]: It's finding the one point that includes everything else.

771
01:02:25,388 --> 01:02:28,409
[SPEAKER_00]: Not finding the point that excludes everything else.

772
01:02:28,749 --> 01:02:33,571
[SPEAKER_01]: So, concentration means being fully established and steady in that background that I'm talking about.

773
01:02:33,731 --> 01:02:34,031
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

774
01:02:34,171 --> 01:02:39,553
[SPEAKER_01]: When you're concentrated, it's when your mind is settled in that background, and no matter what actually you're doing,

775
01:02:39,973 --> 01:02:45,777
[SPEAKER_01]: What things are attacking you, harassing you, coming your way, pleasing you, displeasing you, that concentration remains steady.

776
01:02:46,137 --> 01:02:46,798
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, I'm all.

777
01:02:47,218 --> 01:02:50,660
[SPEAKER_01]: And so, we always use those descriptions of unshakable and so on and so forth.

778
01:02:51,421 --> 01:02:53,502
[SPEAKER_01]: So, because it's fully established in this.

779
01:02:53,522 --> 01:02:55,303
[SPEAKER_01]: So, whatever is coming, it still stays.

780
01:02:55,763 --> 01:02:57,044
[SPEAKER_01]: The mind is concentrated.

781
01:02:57,244 --> 01:02:59,266
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's about taking everything like...

782
01:02:59,286 --> 01:03:00,947
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about becoming so established.

783
01:03:01,207 --> 01:03:05,050
[SPEAKER_01]: It's about, well, again, becoming so... stepping back.

784
01:03:05,510 --> 01:03:05,910
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

785
01:03:06,551 --> 01:03:08,712
[SPEAKER_01]: So much that you get really, really settled.

786
01:03:09,223 --> 01:03:09,943
[SPEAKER_01]: In that background.

787
01:03:10,603 --> 01:03:12,464
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is no concentration without mindfulness.

788
01:03:13,304 --> 01:03:17,546
[SPEAKER_01]: If the mind... if the concentration is about focusing and not seeing anything else, that's a... that's not concentration.

789
01:03:17,746 --> 01:03:26,229
[SPEAKER_01]: The concentration in the suttas is the concentration where you're so mindful, that even when you're not making effort to be mindful, you're still mindful of that.

790
01:03:27,549 --> 01:03:36,672
[SPEAKER_00]: But, eh... Narada Mahārāja said that, no matter how far the patujana reflects, that there's still an aspect of ignorance in that reflection.

791
01:03:38,278 --> 01:03:47,986
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, which is why he has to take it on artificially, and start looking for what he reflects upon as impermanent, as suffering, and then as his experience is not...

792
01:03:48,006 --> 01:03:49,488
[SPEAKER_01]: He doesn't see any of that.

793
01:03:49,808 --> 01:03:57,134
[SPEAKER_01]: He starts emulating it from inside, and if he does it correctly, and if it corresponds to things the way they are, it will take...

794
01:03:57,174 --> 01:04:01,838
[SPEAKER_01]: So, he refers to it as a graft, an alien graft, and then it takes over eventually.

795
01:04:03,251 --> 01:04:11,756
[SPEAKER_00]: So, then, in formal meditation, I find myself often, like, clamping up and trying to focus really hard on the body or the breath, but instead... No, just find your body is already there breathing.

796
01:04:11,976 --> 01:04:12,736
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, yeah, yeah.

797
01:04:13,316 --> 01:04:14,177
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's a valid thought.

798
01:04:14,197 --> 01:04:15,638
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, it's just there.

799
01:04:15,658 --> 01:04:18,779
[SPEAKER_00]: You don't have to go grasp it or reach out for it.

800
01:04:18,959 --> 01:04:19,179
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

801
01:04:19,360 --> 01:04:22,941
[SPEAKER_01]: And the mind will always, inevitably, be attending to something.

802
01:04:23,062 --> 01:04:23,362
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

803
01:04:23,682 --> 01:04:25,063
[SPEAKER_01]: And it doesn't matter what it is.

804
01:04:25,263 --> 01:04:25,563
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

805
01:04:25,763 --> 01:04:26,303
[SPEAKER_01]: In that sense.

806
01:04:26,403 --> 01:04:29,805
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, if you're mindful of your body, you don't have to worry about... in that correct sense.

807
01:04:29,845 --> 01:04:31,306
[SPEAKER_01]: If you find your body present there,

808
01:04:31,958 --> 01:04:36,420
[SPEAKER_01]: Mindful that you don't have to worry about what exactly you're thinking that second, on a particular level.

809
01:04:36,640 --> 01:04:57,151
[SPEAKER_00]: Because you have to be thinking something, so... And then, being aware of thoughts, like, when you're thinking, it takes up a lot of your mental focus and energy, but you still have to have some reflection... Well, again, I think, you know, if mostly attention is gone, dedicated to whatever you're thinking about,

810
01:04:57,567 --> 01:04:59,428
[SPEAKER_01]: Still, you know you're there alive.

811
01:04:59,468 --> 01:05:01,448
[SPEAKER_01]: This random body is still living and functioning.

812
01:05:01,468 --> 01:05:01,769
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

813
01:05:02,249 --> 01:05:05,150
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's... that is the reason for you being able to think in the first place.

814
01:05:05,970 --> 01:05:07,471
[SPEAKER_01]: So, having that little knowledge is enough.

815
01:05:08,911 --> 01:05:18,394
[SPEAKER_01]: Because no matter how much you're caught up in your thoughts, if this body is not there present, alive, on its own, completely indifferent to your thoughts, those thoughts wouldn't be there.

816
01:05:18,775 --> 01:05:19,215
[SPEAKER_01]: They couldn't.

817
01:05:19,495 --> 01:05:20,135
[SPEAKER_01]: Inconceivable.

818
01:05:24,602 --> 01:05:35,044
[SPEAKER_02]: But when I do ānāpānasati, then the, the automatically, you should raise it as interest, as you think, as you thought, but, oh, it's not very, automatically reduced.

819
01:05:35,144 --> 01:05:36,904
[SPEAKER_02]: Sometimes it's just only the thought.

820
01:05:36,924 --> 01:05:37,344
[SPEAKER_02]: Well, no.

821
01:05:37,384 --> 01:05:39,385
[SPEAKER_01]: Particular thought is reduced.

822
01:05:39,825 --> 01:05:40,785
[SPEAKER_01]: Thoughts are not reduced.

823
01:05:41,725 --> 01:05:51,607
[SPEAKER_01]: They can just be, like, slower, or whatever else, but it's not reduced, because your particular thoughts about this might disappear, but the fact that you're aware of your experience as a whole, breathing,

824
01:05:52,095 --> 01:05:53,896
[SPEAKER_01]: Means, you're thinking that.

825
01:05:55,236 --> 01:05:58,017
[SPEAKER_01]: That's being thought.

826
01:05:58,498 --> 01:06:04,220
[SPEAKER_02]: What I'm thinking, thinking about the... What I'm thinking about is the breath.

827
01:06:04,440 --> 01:06:05,941
[SPEAKER_02]: What about how it becomes like that?

828
01:06:06,881 --> 01:06:09,062
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just thinking about the breath only.

829
01:06:09,122 --> 01:06:12,003
[SPEAKER_02]: It's a little, suppose, just not thinking much.

830
01:06:12,023 --> 01:06:13,424
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you can think about the breath.

831
01:06:13,944 --> 01:06:21,847
[SPEAKER_01]: For as long as you are still established mindfully upon the experiences of... upon that background, upon... of your body breathing,

832
01:06:23,382 --> 01:06:31,350
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you're just thinking what's right in front of you, you're trying to turn yourself into a robot and it will not work.

833
01:06:33,633 --> 01:06:35,195
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you're not mindful.

834
01:06:35,495 --> 01:06:37,878
[SPEAKER_01]: You're mindful only in reference to the background.

835
01:06:38,398 --> 01:06:39,379
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what mindfulness is.

836
01:06:40,140 --> 01:06:42,543
[SPEAKER_01]: If you're just bringing things forward, that's not mindfulness.

837
01:06:45,990 --> 01:06:50,832
[SPEAKER_02]: Some people, when they just want to practice jhāna... That's not jhāna either, yeah.

838
01:06:50,852 --> 01:07:00,497
[SPEAKER_01]: Jhāna is being fully established in that background, to the extent where the domain of... you step outside of the domain of sensuality, the first jhāna.

839
01:07:01,118 --> 01:07:03,459
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, the domain of thought in the second jhāna.

840
01:07:05,460 --> 01:07:08,742
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're not anymore thinking about this thought or that thought.

841
01:07:08,862 --> 01:07:13,504
[SPEAKER_02]: Means... and... Yeah, I think, yeah, we can.

842
01:07:16,142 --> 01:07:17,863
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not thinking about this thought or that thought.

843
01:07:17,923 --> 01:07:19,724
[SPEAKER_01]: It means the nature of thinking is there.

844
01:07:21,125 --> 01:07:22,586
[SPEAKER_01]: Nature of a thought.

845
01:07:23,226 --> 01:07:25,167
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's very very general, as you can see.

846
01:07:25,247 --> 01:07:28,749
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just completely non-specific, yet it's real as such.

847
01:07:29,950 --> 01:07:31,911
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what I mean when I say the background.

848
01:07:33,492 --> 01:07:34,392
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's the first jhāna.

849
01:07:34,652 --> 01:07:36,253
[SPEAKER_01]: The second jhāna goes even beyond that.

850
01:07:36,913 --> 01:07:39,575
[SPEAKER_01]: Goes beyond the domain of the nature of thought.

851
01:07:43,867 --> 01:07:56,250
[SPEAKER_02]: In the subtle world, with the daily activities, sometimes when I feel a little... like... sometimes I feel like there's so many... like too much thinking sometimes.

852
01:07:56,350 --> 01:07:57,270
[SPEAKER_02]: So much of a thought.

853
01:07:57,330 --> 01:08:03,131
[SPEAKER_02]: And I... if I just want to reduce a thought, just this... Don't reduce the thought.

854
01:08:03,171 --> 01:08:05,732
[SPEAKER_01]: Reduce your emotional involvement with that thought.

855
01:08:07,332 --> 01:08:11,233
[SPEAKER_01]: If you try interfering with your thoughts, you just try... you end up thinking more.

856
01:08:12,133 --> 01:08:12,833
[SPEAKER_01]: That's our point.

857
01:08:13,763 --> 01:08:16,243
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you'll be worse than before.

858
01:08:18,244 --> 01:08:28,826
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you're mindful of your body being present there while you're thinking, it can give you enough space to not be fully, completely immersed in whatever your mind is thinking.

859
01:08:30,186 --> 01:08:30,686
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's all.

860
01:08:30,706 --> 01:08:31,166
[SPEAKER_01]: That's enough.

861
01:08:31,186 --> 01:08:34,487
[SPEAKER_01]: You just have to be patient with that and it will be recognized that it's enough.

862
01:08:34,547 --> 01:08:34,787
[SPEAKER_01]: Why?

863
01:08:34,807 --> 01:08:40,868
[SPEAKER_01]: Because no matter how hard your mind is working, for as long as you're not emotionally disturbed, it's absolutely fine.

864
01:08:41,488 --> 01:08:42,768
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if it's horrible thoughts,

865
01:08:43,399 --> 01:08:45,081
[SPEAKER_01]: Even if it's thoughts that you don't want to have.

866
01:08:46,762 --> 01:08:48,043
[SPEAKER_01]: Emotionally, you're not involved.

867
01:08:48,303 --> 01:08:49,164
[SPEAKER_01]: That's your concern.

868
01:08:49,785 --> 01:08:52,347
[SPEAKER_01]: Because whatever thoughts have a reason, they will have to cease.

869
01:08:53,588 --> 01:08:58,533
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you try to interfere with them before, means, oh, well, you've taken that domain of thought as yours.

870
01:08:58,953 --> 01:09:02,016
[SPEAKER_01]: You think you have say in what you should be thinking and so on.

871
01:09:02,456 --> 01:09:03,737
[SPEAKER_01]: So you start interfering with it.

872
01:09:06,053 --> 01:09:08,594
[SPEAKER_02]: Sometimes I, like, a little contemplate.

873
01:09:08,614 --> 01:09:14,656
[SPEAKER_02]: Whenever any, like, suffering arises, at that time, actually, more, like, identification is there.

874
01:09:14,796 --> 01:09:22,039
[SPEAKER_01]: So, when I feel any kind of suffering... No, the fact that suffering has arisen means the identification was there beforehand.

875
01:09:22,679 --> 01:09:25,800
[SPEAKER_01]: That's already, you know, like a symptom of the underlying problem.

876
01:09:27,621 --> 01:09:30,082
[SPEAKER_02]: Hmm.

877
01:09:30,122 --> 01:09:30,762
[SPEAKER_01]: Any more, eh?

878
01:09:31,912 --> 01:09:34,273
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the symptom of the underlying problem.

879
01:09:34,454 --> 01:09:40,337
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not that that's when your identification happens, and you have to catch it, or something like that.

880
01:09:40,417 --> 01:09:40,617
[SPEAKER_02]: No.

881
01:09:40,977 --> 01:09:46,821
[SPEAKER_02]: So, for you, in your mind, if lots of thoughts appear, no problem at all, right?

882
01:09:46,961 --> 01:09:48,081
[SPEAKER_02]: Yes, your mind...

883
01:09:48,101 --> 01:09:49,262
[SPEAKER_01]: They were never a problem, yeah.

884
01:09:49,722 --> 01:09:55,305
[SPEAKER_02]: How do you, how do you still, like, whatever arisen into the sea?

885
01:09:55,525 --> 01:09:56,846
[SPEAKER_02]: You contemplate on it, or...?

886
01:09:56,866 --> 01:10:00,128
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you just, again, you stop concerning yourself with the particulars

887
01:10:00,602 --> 01:10:01,782
[SPEAKER_01]: Unless there is a reason for it.

888
01:10:02,643 --> 01:10:04,563
[SPEAKER_01]: You just recognize there is a nature of thinking.

889
01:10:07,324 --> 01:10:12,285
[SPEAKER_01]: You can go out if you want.

890
01:10:16,766 --> 01:10:17,926
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is a nature of thinking.

891
01:10:18,086 --> 01:10:18,787
[SPEAKER_01]: Thoughts are there.

892
01:10:19,067 --> 01:10:19,927
[SPEAKER_01]: Doesn't matter what thoughts.

893
01:10:20,547 --> 01:10:21,227
[SPEAKER_01]: Thoughts are there.

894
01:10:21,647 --> 01:10:24,188
[SPEAKER_01]: Means you're already mindful in regard to whatever you're thinking.

895
01:10:26,254 --> 01:10:28,396
[SPEAKER_02]: If you need something stronger to fear, what do you need?

896
01:10:28,596 --> 01:10:29,317
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's the thing.

897
01:10:29,597 --> 01:10:37,583
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then you just endure it, and then, when the fear is gone, you practice even harder in regards to things that are not too powerful and too overwhelming.

898
01:10:38,264 --> 01:10:39,405
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how you develop strength.

899
01:10:40,185 --> 01:10:42,507
[SPEAKER_01]: So, then, when next time fear comes, well, you'll be stronger.

